# ============================================================
#  Character events — fellow students.
#  Intros are `trigger: random` (they introduce the NPC).
#  Everything else is `trigger: social`: drawn from the monthly
#  social slot, only once the NPC has been met.
#  Romance arc per character: spark (generic) -> love >= 35 ->
#  confession -> partner events. See social.grim for generic ones.
# ============================================================

# ================= LYRA VANESHADE =================

@event lyra_intro
title: The Last Copy
class: routine
tone: tense
actor: lyra
when: not met(lyra) and turn >= 2
weight: 30
art: book
tags: social rival
scene: Two hands reaching for the same red-bound book on a library shelf; one hand wears a signet ring with a flame crest.
text: You reach for the last copy of "Foundations of Flame" and a ringed hand gets there first. "I need it more," says a tall girl with crimson hair, not looking at you. "You'll only underline the wrong bits."
> left: Let her have it
  meet lyra
  rel lyra +tiny
  say: "At least you know your place," she says, which is somehow worse than rudeness. Lyra Vaneshade. Everyone knows the name.
> right: Argue for it
  meet lyra
  challenge negotiate easy:
    win:
      rel lyra +medium
      say: You quote chapter three at her. She raises an eyebrow, then hands you the book. "Fine. Return it underlined correctly."
    lose:
      rel lyra -small
      say: She wins the argument in four sentences and leaves with the book. You think of the perfect comeback that night.

@event lyra_letter
title: A Letter With a Black Seal
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) >= 6
weight: 12
art: letter
tags: social
scene: A girl sitting on a window seat in an empty corridor, crushing a letter with a black wax seal in her fist, face turned away.
text: You find Lyra on a window seat with a crumpled letter. Black seal. Her family's. She's not crying; Vaneshades don't. But she's not quite not crying either.
> left: Pretend you didn't see
  mood -tiny
  say: You walk past. Later, she's flawless again, as if nothing happened. Maybe nothing did.
> right: Sit down beside her
  gold -tiny
  rel lyra +large
  spark lyra +tiny
  flag lyra_vulnerable
  say: "Second place," she says eventually. "I came second in the Winter Trials. My mother wants to know who beat me." She almost laughs. "It's always someone."

@event lyra_study_rivalry
title: Top of the Class
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) > -24
weight: 10
repeat: 4
art: scroll
tags: social study rival
scene: Two students at opposite ends of a long library table, surrounded by towers of books, glaring over the tops of them.
text: The professors have posted rankings. Lyra is first. You're close enough to see the back of her head. She notices you noticing.
> left: Suggest studying together
  health -tiny
  lore +small
  rel lyra +small
  say: "Together?" She considers this like a foreign custom. Then she pulls out a chair. She's an excellent, merciless study partner.
> right: Beat her outright
  challenge research easy:
    win:
      study +medium
      rel lyra +small
      renown +small
      say: Next rankings: you're first. Lyra stares at the list for a long time. Then she finds you and says, "Good." She means it.
    lose:
      study +tiny
      rel lyra -tiny
      say: You study until your eyes bleed and come third. Lyra is still first. She doesn't gloat. That's worse.

@event lyra_family_gala
title: The Vaneshade Winter Gala
class: routine
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) >= 18 and month >= 3 and month <= 6
weight: 12
art: crown
tags: social romance
scene: A glittering ballroom in a noble house, candles floating in mid-air, a tall woman in crimson watching the crowd like a hawk.
text: "My family's winter gala," Lyra says, too casually. "I need a guest who won't embarrass me. You'll do. Probably. You'll need proper clothes."
> left: Decline
  rel lyra -tiny
  say: "Of course." A pause. "It doesn't matter." It clearly does.
> right: Go with her (20 gold for clothes)
  gold -medium
  charm +small
  renown +small
  spark lyra +small
  rel lyra +small
  chance 40:
    mood -small
    say: Lyra's mother asks who your parents are, and then asks no further questions at all. Lyra squeezes your hand under the table, hard.
  else:
    mood +medium
    say: You dance, you charm a duke, you don't spill anything. In the carriage home, Lyra falls asleep on your shoulder.

@event lyra_confession
title: Lyra Doesn't Lose
class: milestone
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: spark(lyra) >= 25 and rel(lyra) >= 18 and bond(lyra) != "partner"
weight: 30
art: flame
tags: romance
scene: A girl with crimson hair standing very close in a practice ring at dusk, sparks still drifting from her wand, cheeks flushed.
text: After practice, Lyra doesn't leave. "I don't lose," she says, staring at the scorch marks. "I don't. But I think — " She stops. Starts again. "I think I've lost to you. Say something before I set something on fire."
> left: Let her down gently
  spark lyra -large
  rel lyra +tiny
  say: She nods, sharp and quick. "Understood." She practises alone for a month. Then one day she nods to you in the corridor, and it's almost all right.
> right: Kiss her
  bond lyra partner
  spark lyra +large
  mood +large
  say: Nothing catches fire. Well. Something does, but it's only the practice dummy, and neither of you notices for a while.

@event lyra_family_ultimatum
title: The Ultimatum
class: routine
tone: grim
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: bond(lyra) == "partner" and turn >= 14
weight: 18
art: crown
tags: romance crisis
scene: Lyra holding a letter with a black seal, her other hand clenched around a ring she has just pulled off.
text: Another black-sealed letter. Lyra reads it twice and goes white. "My mother has found out about us. End it, she says, or she ends my inheritance." She looks at you. "Tell me what to do."
> left: "Choose yourself, not them."
  if spark(lyra) >= 50:
    challenge negotiate trivial:
      win:
        rel lyra +large
        spark lyra +medium
        flag lyra_free
        say: She tears the letter in half. Then in quarters. Then she sets the quarters on fire and laughs like she hasn't in years.
      lose:
        rel lyra -small
        spark lyra -medium
        mood -medium
        say: "Easy for you to say," she snaps. She doesn't mean it. She also doesn't take it back.
  else:
    challenge negotiate easy:
      win:
        rel lyra +large
        spark lyra +medium
        flag lyra_free
        say: She tears the letter in half. Then in quarters. Then she sets the quarters on fire and laughs like she hasn't in years.
      lose:
        rel lyra -small
        spark lyra -medium
        mood -medium
        say: "Easy for you to say," she snaps. She doesn't mean it. She also doesn't take it back.
> right: Step back so she doesn't lose everything
  bond lyra ex
  gain heartbroken
  rel lyra +small
  say: You end it before she has to. She doesn't argue. That's how you know how much it costs her.

@event lyra_rival_sabotage
title: Sabotage in Class
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: bond(lyra) == "rival" and rel(lyra) <= -6
weight: 12
art: potion
tags: rival
scene: A cauldron spitting black smoke, a crimson-haired student walking away with a tiny vial hidden in her sleeve.
text: Your perfect potion turns black and starts screaming. Across the room, Lyra is very carefully not looking at you.
> left: Retaliate (Guile)
  challenge deceive trivial:
    win:
      rel lyra -small
      renown +small
      say: Next lesson, her wand produces only bubbles. Pink ones. She knows. You both know. It's war. It's sort of fun.
    lose:
      gain detention
      rel lyra -medium
      say: You're caught slipping something into her bag. She looks genuinely delighted.
> right: Confront her directly
  gold -tiny
  rel lyra +medium
  say: "That was beneath you." She flushes. "...Yes. It was." The next day there's a perfect replacement potion on your desk.

@event lyra_burnout
title: Lyra Falls
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) >= 12 and year >= 2
weight: 10
art: cross
tags: social
scene: A girl collapsed across a library desk among scattered notes, quill still in hand, candle burned down to nothing.
text: You find Lyra face-down on a library desk at dawn, not asleep — out cold. She's been studying for three days straight. "Don't tell anyone," she mumbles when she comes round. "Mother can't know."
> left: Take her to the infirmary anyway
  rel lyra -tiny
  spark lyra +tiny
  say: She's furious. Then she sleeps for nineteen hours. When she wakes up, she says, quietly, "Thank you."
> right: Cover for her and make her rest
  gold -tiny
  rel lyra +medium
  study -tiny
  say: You tell her professors she has a cold and sit by her door with your homework. She sleeps. You keep watch.

# ================= TOBIAS FENNICK =================

@event tobias_intro
title: The Lost Boy
class: windfall
tone: light
actor: tobias
when: not met(tobias) and turn >= 2
weight: 30
art: compass
tags: social
scene: A large, gentle-faced boy leading a crying first-year by the hand down the wrong corridor, both very lost.
text: A big, broad-shouldered boy is leading a crying first-year through the corridors. "Don't worry, I know exactly where the infirmary is," he says, and walks confidently into a broom cupboard.
> left: Point them the right way
  meet tobias
  rel tobias +small
  say: "Ah. Left, you say. Right. I mean, correct." He grins, enormous and sheepish. "Tobias. Turnip scholarship. Thanks."
> right: Walk with them
  meet tobias
  rel tobias +medium
  mood +small
  say: You end up taking the scenic route, and the first-year stops crying because Tobias is telling a very long story about a goat.

@event tobias_homesick
title: Homesick
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: rel(tobias) >= 6
weight: 12
art: leaf
tags: social nature
scene: A dormitory windowsill crowded with clay pots of seedlings, a big boy watering them with a tiny can.
text: Tobias has gone quiet. He's planted seedlings in every cup in the common room. "Harvest at home," he says. "First one I've missed. Ma's doing it alone."
> left: Cheer him up with a joke
  gold -tiny
  rel tobias +small
  say: Your joke is terrible. He laughs anyway, the big rumbling laugh, and that seems to help.
> right: Help him build a window garden
  health -tiny
  rel tobias +small
  alchemy +tiny
  mood +small
  say: By the end of the week the common room smells of tomato leaves. Tobias whistles while he waters them.

@event tobias_bad_harvest
title: The Harvest Failed
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: rel(tobias) >= 15 and turn >= 8 and not flag(tobias_harvest_done)
weight: 14
art: rain
tags: social money
scene: A boy packing a battered trunk in an empty dormitory, a letter with smudged handwriting open on the bed.
text: Tobias is packing. Blight took the harvest. His family needs money, and hands. "Thirty crowns would get them through winter," he says, not asking. "But I haven't got thirty crowns. I've got two arms."
> left: Persuade him to stay and find work here
  flag tobias_harvest_done
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      rel tobias +medium
      say: You walk him to the job board. He signs up for double shifts at the stables and sends every crown home. He stays.
    lose:
      rel tobias +tiny
      mood -small
      say: He listens, nods, and takes the barge in the morning. He's back in two months, thinner and quieter.
> right: Give him thirty crowns
  when: gold >= 30
  flag tobias_harvest_done
  gold -large
  rel tobias +huge
  spark tobias +tiny
  say: He tries to refuse three times. Then he hugs you so hard your spine cracks. "I'll pay you back. Every crown. Every one."
  queue tobias_repays in 6

@event tobias_repays
title: Every Crown
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
actor: tobias
art: pouch
tags: social money
scene: A clumsy hand-stitched pouch of coins and a jar of honey left on a dormitory pillow.
text: A lumpy, hand-stitched pouch on your pillow: thirty crowns exactly, in small coins. And a jar of honey from home. A note in big, careful letters: "TOLD YOU. — T."
> ok: Smile
  gold +large
  rel tobias +small
  mood +small

@event tobias_godparent
title: The Mandrake Baby
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: rel(tobias) >= 9
weight: 10
art: leaf
tags: social nature
scene: A tiny mandrake in a pot wearing a knitted hat, a beaming boy presenting it like a newborn.
text: Tobias presents a flowerpot containing a very small mandrake in a knitted hat. "This is Gerald," he says. "I'd like you to be his godparent." Gerald screams softly.
> left: Politely decline
  rel tobias -tiny
  say: "No pressure," says Tobias, visibly pressured. Gerald glares at you from under his hat.
> right: Accept with honour
  health -tiny
  rel tobias +small
  mood +small
  alchemy +tiny
  say: You are now Gerald's godparent. Gerald bites you. Tobias says this means Gerald loves you.

@event tobias_bullied
title: Tobias and the Prefect
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: met(bram) and rel(tobias) >= 3
weight: 10
art: shield
tags: social rival
scene: A burly prefect mocking a big farm boy in a crowded corridor, students sniggering, the boy's ears bright red.
text: Bram is doing an impression of Tobias's accent in the corridor. People are laughing. Tobias is pretending not to hear, ears burning red.
> left: Stay out of it
  rel tobias -small
  say: Tobias doesn't mention it. He doesn't sit with you at dinner, either.
> right: Step in
  alignment +small
  rel tobias +large
  rel bram -medium
  challenge negotiate easy:
    win:
      renown +small
      say: "Funny," you say. "Do your father next." The laughter turns on Bram. He stalks off. Tobias stares at you in awe.
    lose:
      gain watched
      say: Bram turns his attention to you instead, with interest. Tobias brings you a pie later. A whole pie.

@event tobias_confession
title: A Confession, With Vegetables
class: milestone
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: spark(tobias) >= 25 and rel(tobias) >= 18 and bond(tobias) != "partner"
weight: 30
art: heart
tags: romance
scene: A big boy holding out a perfect pumpkin like an offering in a greenhouse, cheeks scarlet.
text: Tobias corners you in the greenhouse holding a very large pumpkin. "I grew this," he says. "For you. It's the best one. I didn't know how else to — I like you. Like that. I've practised this on the pumpkin. Sorry."
> left: Let him down gently
  spark tobias -large
  rel tobias +small
  say: He nods a lot. "That's all right. That's fine. You can still have the pumpkin." You keep it until it rots, out of loyalty.
> right: Say yes
  bond tobias partner
  spark tobias +large
  mood +large
  say: He drops the pumpkin. It's fine; pumpkins are sturdy. So, it turns out, are his hugs.

@event tobias_picnic
title: A Picnic in the Orchard
class: milestone
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: bond(tobias) == "partner" and month >= 7 and month <= 10
weight: 14
repeat: 10
art: tree
tags: romance nature
scene: A checked blanket under blossoming apple trees, a basket of bread and cheese, two students lying in the dappled light.
text: Tobias has packed a picnic: bread he baked, cheese he begged from the kitchens, apples from the orchard he has befriended. "No exams for six hours," he announces. "I checked."
> left: Bring your books anyway
  health -tiny
  lore +small
  spark tobias -tiny
  say: You study on the blanket. He falls asleep with his head in your lap. It's still lovely.
> right: Leave everything behind
  gold -tiny
  mood +medium
  health +small
  spark tobias +small
  say: The afternoon goes golden and slow. You can't remember the last time you didn't think about grades.

# ================= SERAPHINE HALE =================

@event seraphine_intro
title: Your Left Shoe
class: windfall
tone: eerie
actor: seraphine
when: not met(seraphine) and turn >= 2
weight: 30
art: eye
tags: social mystery
scene: A slight girl with silver-grey eyes and a scarf of stars passing in a corridor, pointing absently at someone's feet.
text: A girl drifts past you in the corridor and says, without stopping, "You're going to lose your left shoe today. Don't worry, it's under the stairs in the east wing."
> left: Ignore her
  meet seraphine
  say: That afternoon a staircase moves and eats your left shoe. It is, eventually, under the stairs in the east wing.
> right: Ask how she knows
  meet seraphine
  rel seraphine +medium
  say: "I don't know things," she says. "Things know me." Then: "Seraphine. You'll want the shoe back by four." You get it back at 3:58.

@event seraphine_tarot
title: The Cards
class: routine
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: seraphine
when: rel(seraphine) >= 3
weight: 12
art: cards
tags: social mystery
scene: A tarot spread on a velvet cloth in candlelight, a girl's pale fingers turning over a card showing a lightning-struck tower.
text: Seraphine shuffles a battered tarot deck. "One card," she says. "For you. Only if you want it. They're quite rude sometimes."
> left: Draw a card
  chance 50:
    mood +small
    renown +tiny
    say: The Star. "Hope," she says, delighted. "And someone's going to tell you a secret. Oh — it's me. I like you." She blushes.
    rel seraphine +small
  else:
    mood -tiny
    say: The Tower. She looks at it a long time. "It's fine," she says. "Towers fall. That's what they're for."
    rel seraphine +small
> right: Decline
  rel seraphine +tiny
  say: "Good," she says, putting the deck away. "Knowing is overrated."

@event seraphine_lake_vision
title: She Walks Into the Lake
class: story
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: seraphine
when: rel(seraphine) >= 6 and month >= 3 and month <= 9
weight: 10
art: wave
tags: social danger
scene: A girl in a nightgown wading into a misty lake at night, eyes glowing silver, arms outstretched toward something under the water.
text: From your window you see Seraphine walking into the lake in her nightgown, eyes shining silver, already up to her waist.
> left: Wake a prefect
  rel seraphine +small
  say: The prefect drags her out, coughing. She doesn't remember anything. She looks at you strangely for days.
> right: Run down and pull her out
  challenge feat trivial:
    win:
      rel seraphine +large
      spark seraphine +small
      alignment +small
      say: You reach her just as she goes under. On the shore she wakes and whispers, "It was calling me. It called you too." Then she holds on very tight.
    lose:
      health -large
      gain sick
      rel seraphine +large
      say: You both nearly drown. You both come down with Lake Fever. She brings you soup that tastes faintly of the future.

@event seraphine_future
title: I Saw You Old
class: routine
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: seraphine
when: rel(seraphine) >= 15
weight: 10
art: hourglass
tags: social mystery
scene: Two students sitting on the rim of a dry fountain, one looking up at the stars, the other looking at the first with a soft smile.
text: "I saw you old," Seraphine says suddenly. "Last night. You were happy. Really happy. There was someone with you." She pauses. "Do you want to know who?"
> left: Yes, tell me
  chance 50:
    spark seraphine +small
    say: She looks at you for a long time. "I'll tell you when you're old," she says, and goes pink.
  else:
    mood +small
    say: "Someone kind," she says. "That's all I could see. Their hands were kind."
> right: No, let it be a surprise
  gold -tiny
  rel seraphine +medium
  mood +small
  say: She smiles like you've given her a present. "That's the right answer. Nobody ever gives the right answer."

@event seraphine_overwhelmed
title: Too Many Tomorrows
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: seraphine
when: rel(seraphine) >= 9 and year >= 2
weight: 10
art: eye
tags: social
scene: A girl curled in a dark corner of an observatory with her hands over her eyes, a teacup gone cold beside her.
text: Seraphine hasn't come to class in a week. You find her in a dark storeroom with her hands over her eyes. "It's too loud," she whispers. "Everyone's futures. All at once."
> left: Fetch Sister Amaranth
  rel seraphine +small
  say: Amaranth gives her a sleeping draught and a dark room. She recovers. She doesn't say much about it.
> right: Sit with her in the dark
  rel seraphine +large
  spark seraphine +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: You don't speak. After an hour she takes her hands from her eyes. "Yours is quiet," she says. "Your future. It's very quiet. I like it."

@event seraphine_confession
title: She Already Knew
class: milestone
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: seraphine
when: spark(seraphine) >= 25 and rel(seraphine) >= 18 and bond(seraphine) != "partner"
weight: 30
art: star
tags: romance
scene: A girl with silver eyes holding out a single falling-star seed in her palm on a dark observatory balcony.
text: "I've seen this conversation forty-one times," Seraphine says. "In twenty-nine of them, you say yes. I've been very nervous about the other twelve." She holds out her hand. "I like you. That part was always the same."
> left: Gently say no
  spark seraphine -large
  rel seraphine +tiny
  say: She nods. "Twelve," she says softly. "I knew it might be twelve." She's kind to you afterwards. Somehow that hurts more.
> right: Take her hand
  bond seraphine partner
  spark seraphine +large
  mood +large
  say: "Twenty-nine," she whispers, and laughs, and for once she's entirely in the present.

# ================= CORVIN ASHBY =================

@event corvin_intro
title: Light Fingers
class: routine
tone: light
actor: corvin
when: not met(corvin) and turn >= 2
weight: 30
art: mask
tags: social
scene: A dark-haired student with a crooked grin holding up a purse between two fingers, mid-bow.
text: Someone bumps you in the crowd. A moment later a dark-haired boy is bowing and holding up your purse. "You dropped this," he says. "Into my pocket. Terrible habit of yours. Corvin Ashby."
> left: Snatch it back and report him
  meet corvin
  rel corvin -small
  say: He's gone before the prefect arrives. Your purse is lighter by exactly one crown and heavier by one IOU.
> right: Laugh
  health -tiny
  meet corvin
  rel corvin +medium
  guile +tiny
  say: "Oh, I like you," he says, and teaches you the trick on the spot. You practise it on him. He lets you win. Probably.

@event corvin_kitchen_raid
title: The Kitchen Raid
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: rel(corvin) >= 3
weight: 12
art: meal
tags: social
scene: Two students creeping through a cavernous castle kitchen at night, a mountain of tarts on a table, a sleeping cook snoring by the hearth.
text: "Midnight," Corvin whispers. "The cooks have made forty treacle tarts for the faculty dinner. Forty. Nobody needs forty."
> left: Not tonight
  rel corvin -tiny
  say: He goes alone. The next morning there's a treacle tart on your pillow. You decide not to ask.
> right: Lead the raid
  challenge deceive trivial:
    win:
      mood +medium
      rel corvin +medium
      say: You get out with nine tarts and a bottle of elderflower cordial. You eat them on the roof until sunrise.
    lose:
      gain detention
      rel corvin +medium
      say: The cook wakes up. You both spend a week scrubbing pans, laughing too hard to work.

@event corvin_debt
title: Corvin's Little Problem
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: rel(corvin) >= 12 and not flag(corvin_owes) and not flag(corvin_debt_refused)
weight: 12
art: chain
tags: social money
scene: A boy with a black eye sitting on the dormitory stairs, trying very hard to look casual.
text: Corvin has a black eye and a very casual expression. "Small misunderstanding with some trolls," he says. "Thirty crowns would clear it right up. I'll pay you back. Probably with interest. Possibly with a goat."
> left: Refuse
  flag corvin_debt_refused
  rel corvin -medium
  say: "Course. No problem." He has another black eye the next week. He's still friendly. Mostly.
> right: Give him thirty crowns
  when: gold >= 30
  gold -large
  flag corvin_owes
  rel corvin +large
  queue corvin_repays in 4
  say: He stares at the coins, then at you. "No one's ever just... done that." He's quiet for a whole minute. A record.

@event corvin_repays
title: Interest
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
actor: corvin
art: coin
tags: social money
scene: A small brass key and a fat purse left on a desk with a playing card, the jack of spades, tucked under them.
text: There's a fat purse on your desk and a jack of spades tucked under it. Inside the purse: more than thirty crowns. Much more.
> left: Count it
  chance 70:
    gold +huge
    rel corvin +medium
    say: Fifty-five crowns. A note: "Interest. Don't ask. — C." You don't ask.
  else:
    gold +tiny
    rel corvin +small
    say: Five crowns and a very convincing IOU for the other twenty-five, with a doodle of a goat.
> right: Find him and ask where it came from
  rel corvin +large
  gold +large
  say: "I won it," he says. "Fairly. Mostly." He pushes the exact thirty into your hand. "The rest's mine. I've got another debt to pay."

@event corvin_rooftop
title: Up on the Roof
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: rel(corvin) >= 18
weight: 10
art: moon
tags: social
scene: Two students sitting on a steep slate roof under a full moon, legs dangling over a dizzying drop, sharing a bottle of something fizzy.
text: On the roof at 2am, Corvin goes quiet. "I'm on my last warning," he says. "One more detention and they send me home. And home is... not a good place." He laughs, badly.
> left: Tell him to keep his head down
  gold -tiny
  rel corvin +small
  say: "Head down. Right. I'll try anything once." He keeps his head down for almost a month.
> right: Promise you'll cover for him
  gold -tiny
  rel corvin +large
  spark corvin +tiny
  flag covering_corvin
  say: He looks at you like nobody has ever promised him anything. "You're an idiot," he says. "Thank you."

@event corvin_framed
title: Corvin Is Framed
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: rel(corvin) >= 9 and met(bram) and turn >= 10
weight: 10
art: scales
tags: social rival
scene: A boy standing before a disciplinary desk, a stolen silver goblet on it, a smug prefect at his shoulder.
text: The headmistress's silver goblet has been found in Corvin's trunk. He swears he didn't take it. Bram, who found it, looks very pleased. Corvin is one detention from expulsion.
> left: Stay out of it
  rel corvin -large
  chance 50:
    say: Corvin talks his way out, barely. He doesn't look at you for a month.
  else:
    rel corvin -large
    say: Corvin is suspended for a month. When he comes back, he's different. Quieter.
> right: Find proof he was framed (Guile)
  challenge deceive trivial:
    win:
      rel corvin +large
      rel bram -large
      renown +small
      say: You find the bill of sale: Bram bought a fake. Bram is stripped of his sash. Corvin buys you a goat. An actual goat.
    lose:
      rel corvin +medium
      gain watched
      say: You can't prove it. But you stood up for him in front of everyone, and he'll never forget it. Neither will Bram.

@event corvin_confession
title: Corvin, Serious for Once
class: milestone
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: spark(corvin) >= 25 and rel(corvin) >= 18 and bond(corvin) != "partner"
weight: 30
art: cards
tags: romance
scene: A boy holding out a playing card — the queen of hearts — with an unsteady hand, no grin for once.
text: Corvin holds out a playing card. The queen of hearts. His hand isn't quite steady. "No trick," he says. "No angle. I just — I like you more than I like anything, and I'm terrified, and I wanted you to have this."
> left: Gently decline
  spark corvin -large
  rel corvin +tiny
  say: He laughs, too quickly. "Worth a shot." He keeps the card. You see it sometimes, tucked in his sleeve.
> right: Take the card
  bond corvin partner
  spark corvin +large
  mood +large
  say: For once, Corvin Ashby has nothing to say. He just kisses you, and then grins, and then can't stop grinning.

@event corvin_runaway
title: Let's Leave Tonight
class: story
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: bond(corvin) == "partner" and final_year
weight: 16
art: map
tags: romance danger
scene: A small sky-barge tied to the academy dock at midnight, lanterns lit, a boy at the tiller holding out his hand.
text: Corvin's at your door at midnight, bag over his shoulder. "There's a sky-barge at the dock and nobody guarding it. Let's go. Tonight. The world's huge and we're wasting it in classrooms."
> left: Stay and finish what you started
  rel corvin -small
  spark corvin +tiny
  say: He looks at you for a long time. Then he drops the bag. "Fine. But after graduation, we steal a boat. A big one."
> right: Take his hand
  end ending_runaway

# ================= MIRA TEN =================

@event mira_intro
title: An Explosion in the West Wing
class: routine
tone: light
actor: mira
when: not met(mira) and turn >= 2
weight: 30
art: gear
tags: social
scene: A cloud of purple smoke billowing from a workshop door, a soot-covered student emerging with goggles and a thumbs-up.
text: The west wing explodes. Not badly. A figure in goggles stumbles out of the purple smoke, coughing, and gives you a thumbs-up. "Don't worry! That was intentional! Mostly! Can you hold this?" They hand you a ticking teapot.
> left: Put the teapot down and back away
  meet mira
  rel mira +tiny
  say: The teapot stops ticking and starts humming the academy anthem. "Mira," they say. "They/them. Thanks for not throwing it."
> right: Hold the teapot steady
  meet mira
  challenge brew trivial:
    win:
      rel mira +medium
      say: You keep it level while they twist a valve. It stops ticking. "You've got good hands," Mira says. "I'm going to need those."
    lose:
      health -tiny
      rel mira +medium
      say: The teapot goes off. Your eyebrows survive, mostly. Mira is apologising and laughing at the same time.

@event mira_owl_gift
title: A Present With Gears
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: mira
when: rel(mira) >= 18 and not has(familiar_owl)
weight: 14
art: owl
tags: social magic
scene: A small brass owl with glowing amber eyes perched on a student's wrist, its clockwork feathers fluffing.
text: Mira presents a brass owl with amber glass eyes. It blinks, hoots the hour and says "HOMEWORK" in a tinny voice. "Made it for you. It remembers deadlines. And birthdays. And grudges, slightly."
> left: It's too much
  gold -tiny
  rel mira +small
  say: Mira looks crushed, then rallies. "I'll give it to Thorne. He needs reminding to smile." The owl, you hear, refuses to work for him.
> right: Accept it gratefully
  gold -tiny
  gain familiar_owl
  rel mira +medium
  spark mira +tiny
  say: The owl settles on your shoulder and says, "WELCOME." Mira pretends to have something in their eye.

@event mira_fair
title: The Artificers' Fair
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: mira
when: rel(mira) >= 9 and month >= 6 and month <= 9
weight: 12
art: gear
tags: social festival
scene: A hall crammed with bizarre inventions — walking teapots, singing clocks — and one enormous brass machine draped in a sheet.
text: The Artificers' Fair. Mira's entry is under a sheet and occasionally growls. "I need an assistant to stand next to it and look confident," they say. "And possibly run."
> left: Watch from a safe distance
  gold -tiny
  mood +small
  rel mira +tiny
  say: The machine turns out to be a mechanical bear that bakes bread. It wins second place. Mira is ecstatic and flour-covered.
> right: Be the confident assistant
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      renown +medium
      rel mira +medium
      say: You present it like a showman. The bear bakes a perfect loaf and bows. First prize. Mira kisses the trophy, then, in a fluster, your cheek.
      spark mira +tiny
    lose:
      health -small
      renown +small
      rel mira +small
      say: The bear eats your sleeve. The crowd loves it. Third prize and a very good story.

@event mira_workshop_closed
title: The Workshop Is Shut
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: mira
when: rel(mira) >= 12 and year >= 2
weight: 10
art: lock
tags: social
scene: A workshop door chained shut with a faculty notice nailed to it, a forlorn student sitting on a toolbox outside.
text: After the third fire this term, the faculty has padlocked Mira's workshop. Mira is sitting on a toolbox outside it, looking like someone took their heart and filed it under "hazards".
> left: Plead their case to Professor Thorne
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      rel mira +large
      rel thorne +tiny
      say: Thorne agrees to reopen it — with fire buckets and a weekly inspection. Mira cries on you. Oil and all.
    lose:
      rel mira +small
      rel thorne -tiny
      say: Thorne refuses. But Mira heard you try. "Nobody's ever argued for me before," they say.
> right: Help them build a secret workshop
  challenge deceive trivial:
    win:
      rel mira +large
      guile +tiny
      say: An abandoned classroom behind a tapestry. You bring candles; Mira brings everything else. It's perfect. It's almost entirely fireproof.
    lose:
      rel mira +medium
      gain detention
      say: Bram finds the secret workshop on day two. Worth it, says Mira, scrubbing cauldrons beside you.

@event mira_dance_machine
title: The Dancing Machine
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: mira
when: rel(mira) >= 6
weight: 10
art: music
tags: social
scene: A spindly brass contraption with too many legs attempting a waltz in an empty classroom, a student dancing with it.
text: Mira has built a machine that teaches dancing. It has six legs and opinions. "It needs a test subject," they say. "It's mostly safe. It only kicked me twice."
> left: Make Mira test it
  gold -tiny
  rel mira +small
  mood +small
  say: You watch Mira and the machine waltz, badly, across the room. It's the funniest thing you've ever seen.
> right: Dance with the machine
  charm +small
  health -tiny
  rel mira +medium
  say: It kicks you twice too. But by the end you can waltz, and Mira is clapping with oily hands.

@event mira_confession
title: Blueprint
class: milestone
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: mira
when: spark(mira) >= 25 and rel(mira) >= 18 and bond(mira) != "partner"
weight: 30
art: gear
tags: romance
scene: A rolled-out blueprint on a workbench showing a heart-shaped mechanism labelled with tiny careful notes, a nervous artificer beside it.
text: Mira unrolls a blueprint. It's a mechanical heart, labelled in tiny careful handwriting: "Does not work without the other part." They clear their throat. "I'm bad at saying things. So I drew it. You're the other part. If you want."
> left: Kindly say no
  spark mira -large
  rel mira +small
  say: Mira rolls up the blueprint carefully. "Good to know. Data is data." They're fine. They're mostly fine.
> right: "I want."
  bond mira partner
  spark mira +large
  mood +large
  say: The heart doesn't need to work. But Mira builds it anyway, and it ticks on your windowsill, in time with your own.

@event mira_family_business
title: The Family Clockworks
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: mira
when: rel(mira) >= 15 and year >= 2 and not flag(mira_family_done)
weight: 10
art: gear
tags: social
scene: An artificer holding a stiff letter embossed with a gear crest, a train ticket tucked inside, staring at it blankly.
text: A letter from Mira's parents: the family clockworks needs them home. A ticket is enclosed. "They think this is a hobby," Mira says. "This. Is. Not. A. Hobby."
> left: Tell them family comes first
  flag mira_family_done
  rel mira -small
  say: Mira goes home for a month and comes back with a new scar and a clearer jaw. "They know now," they say. "It's not a hobby."
> right: Help them write back
  health -tiny
  flag mira_family_done
  rel mira +large
  charm +tiny
  say: Together you write a letter so persuasive it should be framed. Mira's mother replies: "Fine. Win a prize." Mira intends to win all of them.

# ================= NESSA QUILL =================

@event nessa_intro
title: First Impressions
class: routine
tone: light
actor: nessa
when: not met(nessa) and turn >= 2
weight: 30
art: paper
tags: social
scene: A girl with ink-stained fingers and a self-writing quill floating at her shoulder, holding a notebook out expectantly.
text: A girl with a quill floating at her shoulder plants herself in front of you. "Nessa Quill, Lumen Ledger. First impressions of Lumenhold, go. Be interesting, please. The last six were boring."
> left: Give a safe answer
  meet nessa
  rel nessa +tiny
  say: The quill writes "SAFE" in the margin and underlines it twice. Nessa sighs and moves on.
> right: Say something outrageous
  meet nessa
  challenge negotiate easy:
    win:
      renown +small
      rel nessa +medium
      say: You're quoted on the front page. Half the academy now thinks you're hilarious. The other half thinks you're dangerous. Nessa thinks both.
    lose:
      renown +small
      rel nessa +tiny
      mood -tiny
      say: You are quoted. Out of context. Extremely out of context.

@event nessa_gossip_column
title: You're in the Gossip Column
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: nessa
when: renown >= 15
weight: 12
art: paper
tags: social
scene: A copy of the Lumen Ledger pinned to a noticeboard, a gossip column circled in red ink, students gathered round giggling.
text: This week's Ledger gossip column features you, prominently, under the headline "WHO IS THE MYSTERY STUDENT ALWAYS IN THE LIBRARY AT MIDNIGHT?" Nessa swears she didn't write it.
> left: Confront Nessa
  rel nessa -tiny
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      say: She prints a correction. Sort of. It's a much more flattering paragraph about you.
      renown +small
    lose:
      say: "Freedom of the press," says Nessa, sweetly. You both know she wrote it.
> right: Lean into the mystery
  gold -tiny
  renown +small
  mood +small
  rel nessa +small
  say: You start leaving cryptic notes in the library. The column runs for six more weeks. Nessa is delighted.

@event nessa_source
title: The Source
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: nessa
when: rel(nessa) >= 12 and (member(library_assistant) or visits_to(courtyard) >= 3 or rel(thorne) >= 9)
weight: 10
art: feather
tags: social
scene: Two students in a dark corner of the library, one whispering, the other writing furiously in a notebook.
text: Nessa leans in. "You've got faculty access. The professors are planning to change the exam format and they're hiding it. I just need a quote. Anonymous. Please?"
> left: Refuse — that's a breach of trust
  rel nessa -small
  rel thorne +small
  say: Nessa sulks for a day. Then she respects you for it, which she hates.
> right: Give her the scoop
  rel nessa +large
  renown +small
  chance 30:
    rel thorne -large
    say: The story runs. Thorne knows exactly who talked. His glare could curdle milk.
  else:
    say: The story runs. Students are grateful. Nobody knows it was you. Nessa buys you cake.

@event nessa_hollow_story
title: Nessa Smells a Story
class: story
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: nessa
when: clues(hollowstar) >= 1 and rel(nessa) >= 6
weight: 12
art: paper
tags: social mystery hollowstar
scene: A wall in the newspaper office covered in pinned clippings and red string connecting a frozen lake, a black star and a fur-coated boy.
text: Nessa's office wall is covered in red string. In the middle: a sketch of a black star. "Frozen fountains. Missing pages. A transfer from the North. Something's going on and you know about it. Spill."
> left: Warn her off — it's dangerous
  rel nessa -tiny
  say: "That's what people say right before the best stories." But she takes the string down. Mostly.
> right: Share what you know
  rel nessa +medium
  chance 40:
    gain watched
    say: Nessa's article runs with half the facts. The man in grey reads it. So does Bram, who starts following you around.
  else:
    say: Nessa's notes are scarily thorough. She's found a record of three students who vanished in 1723. All on Blossom moons.

@event nessa_paper_threatened
title: Stop the Presses
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: nessa
when: rel(nessa) >= 9 and year >= 2
weight: 10
art: paper
tags: social
scene: A printing press with a faculty seal stamped across it, a defiant student standing in front of it with arms crossed.
text: The headmistress has threatened to shut down the Ledger after an article about faculty salaries. Nessa is organising a protest. "I need people on the steps. Visible people. You."
> left: Stay out of it
  rel nessa -small
  say: The protest is small. The Ledger survives, barely. Nessa notices who wasn't there.
> right: Stand on the steps
  rel nessa +large
  rel isolde -small
  renown +medium
  say: Forty students on the steps, chanting. The headmistress comes out and, astonishingly, listens. The Ledger stays.

@event nessa_confession
title: Off the Record
class: milestone
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: nessa
when: spark(nessa) >= 25 and rel(nessa) >= 18 and bond(nessa) != "partner"
weight: 30
art: feather
tags: romance
scene: A girl with an inkpot in one hand, her self-writing quill hovering above a blank page that she has commanded to stay blank.
text: Nessa puts down her quill. Then she tells it to stop writing. It's the first time you've seen it still. "This is off the record," she says. "Completely. I like you. I've drafted this eleven times. None of the drafts were good enough."
> left: Gently say no
  spark nessa -large
  rel nessa +tiny
  say: "Noted," she says crisply. She keeps her quill still a moment longer. Then it starts writing again, and so does she.
> right: Kiss her
  bond nessa partner
  spark nessa +large
  mood +large
  say: Her quill, unattended, writes a single word in the margin: "FINALLY."
